.Dd 2026-11-08
.Dt LBTS-SYNC 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts sync
.Nd synchronize the tickets with other clones of a git repository
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm lbts sync
.Op Fl -no-push
.Sh DESCRIPTION
For an instance that is stored in git, see
.Xr lbts-init 1 ,
this command sends the changes to the tickets to the remote repository,
and receives the changes that others made:
.Bl -enum
.It
It commits any changes in
.Pa .lightbts
that were not committed yet,
for example because committing failed when a message was imported.
.It
It pulls from the upstream of the
.Ql lightbts
branch with
.Ql git pull --rebase .
Messages never conflict, since each one is a new file.
If the shared configuration conflicts, the command stops,
and the conflict has to be resolved in
.Pa .lightbts
with git.
.It
It adds the new messages to the index.
Tickets that were created elsewhere get the next free numbers in this instance,
so numbers can differ between clones; IDs are the same everywhere.
.It
It pushes the
.Ql lightbts
branch.
If the branch has no upstream yet, it is pushed to
.Ql origin ,
and becomes the upstream.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -no-push
Only commit and receive changes, don't push them.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts 1 ,
.Xr lbts-init 1 .
.Sh AUTHOR
.An "Guus Sliepen" Aq guus@lightbts.info
